### 2. Backend: Fetch Scheduled Time in Workflow History
Right now, the API that feeds the frontend history doesn't return the SCHEDULED_TIME column from the workflow table. We need to add it to the SQL SELECT.
**Find the getWorkflowHistory method (around line 770) and UPDATE the SQL query:**
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getWorkflowHistory(String batchId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                w.LAST_ACTION_BY, 
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, w.LAST_ACTION_BY) AS ACTION_USER_NAME, 
                w.LAST_ACTION, 
                w.LAST_ACTION_AT, 
                w.REMARKS,
                w.SCHEDULED_TIME   -- <-- Added this line to fetch the time!
            FROM VOUCHER_WORKFLOW w 
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON w.LAST_ACTION_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE w.BATCH_ID_FK = ? 
            ORDER BY w.LAST_ACTION_AT ASC
        """;

        return jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, batchId);
    }

